  "id": "mixed-model",
  "term": "mixed model",
  "definition": "A mixed model is a statistical approach for analyzing data that include repeated measurements or clustered groups while accounting for random effects. In the context described here, it can be extended to handle several related outcomes together, so change over time or differences between groups can be studied within a multilevel framework.",
